  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that scvi_n200 as RNA encoder dramatically outperforms scgpt (0.706 vs ~0.52-0.54) with the same image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), aggregation (avgpool), and fusion (weighted). The current best (config_045) uses imagenet_vit_l, but we have no data on how the image encoder interacts with scvi_n200. config_007 (scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) is the cleanest single-variable test: it changes only the image encoder from the current best, isolating whether resnet50 provides complementary or superior visual features when paired with the scvi_n200 RNA representation. This is the highest-impact untested dimension (image encoder is more fundamental than aggregation, which showed only ~2% difference with scgpt), and resolving it early with 6 experiments remaining will guide the rest of the search toward the best image-RNA pairing."
}

